# Command-line Maven builds write to `target-cli`, keeping `target` for the VS Code Java language
# server (redhat.java / m2e). Sharing one output directory makes the IDE's JDK-21 Eclipse-compiled
# classes overwrite Maven's Java 25 bytecode mid-build, which surfaces as NoClassDefFoundError or
# "Unresolved compilation problems" at test runtime. See the buildDirName comment in pom.xml.
-DbuildDirName=target-cli
